{
  "format": "srwb",
  "format_version": "1.0",
  "exported_at": "2026-08-15T17:20:20.524Z",
  "notebook": {
    "id": "default",
    "name": "Analyse du graphe d'appels et détection des composantes fortement connexes (SCC)",
    "autoNameNumber": null,
    "description": "",
    "kernelLanguage": "prolog",
    "catalogId": null,
    "catalogRevision": null,
    "cellCounter": 38,
    "cells": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "code": "# Analyse du graphe d'appels et détection des composantes fortement connexes (SCC)\n\nCe carnet explore les fonctionnalités avancées d'analyse de code d'UnifyWeaver :\n\n- **Construction du graphe d'appels** - Création de graphes de dépendances à partir de code Prolog\n- **Détection des SCC** - Recherche de composantes fortement connexes (récursion mutuelle)\n- **Analyse des motifs** - Compréhension des motifs de récursion\n- **Visualisation des dépendances** - Représentation visuelle des relations entre prédicats\n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage\n\n- Comprendre comment UnifyWeaver analyse la structure du code\n- Construire et inspecter des graphes d'appels\n- Détecter la récursion mutuelle à l'aide de l'algorithme de Tarjan\n- Visualiser les dépendances de code",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "code": "## Configuration\n\nCharger UnifyWeaver et les modules d'analyse.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "code": "% Charger l'initialisation\n['../init'].\n\n% Charger les modules d'analyse\nuse_module(unifyweaver(core/advanced/call_graph)).\nuse_module(unifyweaver(core/advanced/scc_detection)).\nuse_module(unifyweaver(core/advanced/pattern_matchers)).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Cannot find file: ../init",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Cannot find file: ../init</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 4,
        "code": "## Exemple 1 : Graphe d'appels simple\n\nCommençons par un prédicat simple et construisons son graphe d'appels.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 5,
        "code": "% Définir le prédicat ancestor\n:- dynamic ancestor/2.\n:- dynamic parent/2.\n\n% Faits de parent\nparent(abraham, isaac).\nparent(isaac, jacob).\n\n% Règles de ancestor\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\nancestor(X, Z) :- parent(X, Y), ancestor(Y, Z).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 6,
        "code": "### Construire le graphe d'appels",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 7,
        "code": "% Construire le graphe d'appels pour ancestor\nbuild_call_graph([ancestor/2], _Graph),\nformat('Call Graph for ancestor/2:~n'),\nforall(member(_Edge, _Graph),\n    format('  ~w~n', [_Edge])).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 8,
        "code": "### Analyser les dépendances",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 9,
        "code": "% Obtenir toutes les dépendances de ancestor/2\nget_dependencies(ancestor/2, _Deps),\nformat('Dependencies of ancestor/2: ~w~n', [_Deps]).\n\n% Vérifier si auto-récursif\n(is_self_recursive(ancestor/2) ->\n    writeln('✓ ancestor/2 is self-recursive')\n;\n    writeln('✗ ancestor/2 is not self-recursive')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: get_dependencies/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: get_dependencies/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 10,
        "code": "## Exemple 2 : Détection de récursion mutuelle\n\nDétectons maintenant la récursion mutuelle avec l'exemple pair/impair.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 11,
        "code": "% Définir des prédicats mutuellement récursifs\n:- dynamic is_even/1.\n:- dynamic is_odd/1.\n\nis_even(0).\nis_even(N) :- N > 0, N1 is N - 1, is_odd(N1).\n\nis_odd(1).\nis_odd(N) :- N > 1, N1 is N - 1, is_even(N1).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 12,
        "code": "### Construire le graphe d'appels pour les deux prédicats",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 13,
        "code": "% Construire le graphe d'appels pour les deux prédicats\nbuild_call_graph([is_even/1, is_odd/1], _Graph),\nformat('Call Graph for is_even/1 and is_odd/1:~n'),\nforall(member(_Edge, _Graph),\n    format('  ~w~n', [_Edge])).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 14,
        "code": "### Trouver les composantes fortement connexes (SCC)",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 15,
        "code": "% Reconstruire le graphe car les variables ne persistent pas entre les cellules du carnet\nbuild_call_graph([is_even/1, is_odd/1], _Graph),\n% Trouver les SCC à l'aide de l'algorithme de Tarjan\nfind_sccs(_Graph, _SCCs),\nformat('Strongly Connected Components:~n'),\nforall(member(_SCC, _SCCs),\n    format('  ~w~n', [_SCC])).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 16,
        "code": "### Vérifier si la SCC est triviale",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 17,
        "code": "% Recalculer les valeurs dérivées pour que cette cellule s'exécute aussi indépendamment\nbuild_call_graph([is_even/1, is_odd/1], _Graph),\nfind_sccs(_Graph, _SCCs),\n% Vérifier chaque SCC\nforall(member(_SCC, _SCCs),\n    (   is_trivial_scc(_SCC) ->\n        format('  ~w is trivial (single predicate)~n', [_SCC])\n    ;\n        format('  ~w is NON-TRIVIAL (mutual recursion!)~n', [_SCC])\n    )\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 18,
        "code": "## Exemple 3 : Graphe d'appels complexe\n\nAnalysons un système plus complexe comportant plusieurs prédicats.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 19,
        "code": "% Définir un petit programme avec plusieurs prédicats\n:- dynamic grandparent/2.\n:- dynamic sibling/2.\n:- dynamic cousin/2.\n\n% grandparent utilise parent\ngrandparent(X, Z) :- parent(X, Y), parent(Y, Z).\n\n% sibling : même parent, enfants différents\nsibling(X, Y) :- parent(P, X), parent(P, Y), X \\= Y.\n\n% cousin : les parents sont frères et sœurs\ncousin(X, Y) :- parent(P1, X), parent(P2, Y), sibling(P1, P2).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 20,
        "code": "### Construire le graphe d'appels complet",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 21,
        "code": "% Construire le graphe d'appels pour tous les prédicats\nbuild_call_graph([grandparent/2, sibling/2, cousin/2], _Graph),\nformat('Complete Call Graph:~n'),\nforall(member(_Edge, _Graph),\n    format('  ~w~n', [_Edge])).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 22,
        "code": "### Trouver des groupes de prédicats\n\nTrouver le groupe de prédicats mutuellement récursifs contenant un prédicat de départ.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 23,
        "code": "% Trouver le groupe mutuellement récursif contenant cousin/2\npredicates_in_group(cousin/2, _Group),\nformat('Mutually recursive group containing cousin/2: ~w~n', [_Group]).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: predicates_in_group/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: predicates_in_group/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 24,
        "code": "## Exemple 4 : Détection de motifs\n\nUtilisons les comparateurs de motifs pour analyser les types de récursion.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 25,
        "code": "% Définir différents motifs récursifs\n:- dynamic count/3.     % Récursif terminal\n:- dynamic factorial/2. % Récursif linéaire\n:- dynamic fib/2.       % Récursif arborescent (ou linéaire si détecté)\n\n% Comptage avec récursion terminale\ncount([], Acc, Acc).\ncount([_|T], Acc, N) :-\n    Acc1 is Acc + 1,\n    count(T, Acc1, N).\n\n% Factorielle avec récursion linéaire\nfactorial(0, 1).\nfactorial(N, F) :-\n    N > 0,\n    N1 is N - 1,\n    factorial(N1, F1),\n    F is N * F1.\n\n% Fibonacci (peut être détecté comme linéaire ou arborescent)\nfib(0, 0).\nfib(1, 1).\nfib(N, F) :-\n    N > 1,\n    N1 is N - 1,\n    N2 is N - 2,\n    fib(N1, F1),\n    fib(N2, F2),\n    F is F1 + F2.",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 26,
        "code": "### Détecter la récursion terminale",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 27,
        "code": "% Vérifier si count/3 est récursif terminal\n(is_tail_recursive_accumulator(count/3, _AccInfo) ->\n    format('✓ count/3 is tail recursive: ~w~n', [_AccInfo])\n;\n    writeln('✗ count/3 is not tail recursive')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: is_tail_recursive_accumulator/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: is_tail_recursive_accumulator/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 28,
        "code": "### Détecter la récursion linéaire",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 29,
        "code": "% Vérifier si factorial/2 est récursif linéaire\n(is_linear_recursive_streamable(factorial/2) ->\n    writeln('✓ factorial/2 is linear recursive')\n;\n    writeln('✗ factorial/2 is not linear recursive')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: is_linear_recursive_streamable/1",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: is_linear_recursive_streamable/1</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 30,
        "code": "### Compter les appels récursifs",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 31,
        "code": "% Compter les appels récursifs dans fibonacci\nfunctor(_FibHead, fib, 2),\nuser:clause(_FibHead, _FibBody),\nonce(contains_call_to(_FibBody, fib)),\ncount_recursive_calls(_FibBody, fib, _Count),\nformat('Fibonacci body has ~w recursive calls~n', [_Count]).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "once/1: Unknown procedure: contains_call_to/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">once/1: Unknown procedure: contains_call_to/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 32,
        "code": "## Visualisation au format DOT\n\nGénérons une représentation Graphviz DOT de notre graphe d'appels.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 33,
        "code": "% Fonction d'assistance pour générer le format DOT\ngenerate_dot(Graph, DotCode) :-\n    findall(Line,\n        (   member(From -> To, Graph),\n            format(atom(Line), '  \"~w\" -> \"~w\";', [From, To])\n        ),\n        Lines),\n    atomic_list_concat(['digraph CallGraph {', '  rankdir=LR;' | Lines], '\\n', Body),\n    format(atom(DotCode), '~w~n}~n', [Body]).\n\n% Générer le DOT pour le graphe pair/impair\nbuild_call_graph([is_even/1, is_odd/1], _Graph),\ngenerate_dot(_Graph, _DotCode),\nwriteln('DOT Code for even/odd call graph:'),\nwriteln(_DotCode).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 34,
        "code": "### Enregistrer le fichier DOT",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 35,
        "code": "% Reconstruire le code source DOT car les variables ne persistent pas entre les cellules\nbuild_call_graph([is_even/1, is_odd/1], _Graph),\ngenerate_dot(_Graph, _DotCode),\nsetup_call_cleanup(\n    open('/shared/data/even_odd_graph.dot', write, _Stream),\n    write(_Stream, _DotCode),\n    close(_Stream)),\nwriteln('✓ Saved to /shared/data/even_odd_graph.dot').\n\nwriteln('To visualize, run:'),\nwriteln('  dot -Tpng /shared/data/even_odd_graph.dot -o even_odd_graph.png').",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: build_call_graph/2</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 36,
        "code": "## Exercice : Analysez votre propre code\n\nEssayez de définir vos propres prédicats et de les analyser !",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 37,
        "code": "% Définissez vos prédicats ici\n% Construisez ensuite les graphes d'appels, trouvez les SCC et détectez les motifs\n\n% Exemple :\n% :- dynamic my_predicate/2.\n% my_predicate(...) :- ...\n\n% build_call_graph([my_predicate/2], Graph).\n",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 38,
        "code": "## Résumé\n\nDans ce carnet, vous avez appris :\n\n✅ Comment construire des graphes d'appels à partir de code Prolog\n\n✅ Comment détecter les composantes fortement connexes (SCC) pour la récursion mutuelle\n\n✅ Comment utiliser les comparateurs de motifs pour classifier les types de récursion\n\n✅ Comment analyser les dépendances de prédicats\n\n✅ Comment visualiser les graphes d'appels au format DOT\n\n## Sujets avancés\n\nPour aller plus loin dans l'analyse :\n\n- **Tri topologique** : Utiliser `topological_order/2` pour ordonner les SCC par dépendances\n- **Comparateurs de motifs personnalisés** : Écrire vos propres prédicats de détection de motifs\n- **Extraction de motif d'accumulateur** : Utiliser `extract_accumulator_pattern/2` pour une analyse détaillée\n- **Interdire la récursion linéaire** : Utiliser `forbid_linear_recursion/1` pour forcer d'autres stratégies de compilation\n\n## Références et fichiers associés\n\n- Chapitre 10 : Introspection et théorie Prolog\n- `src/unifyweaver/core/advanced/call_graph.pl`\n- `src/unifyweaver/core/advanced/scc_detection.pl`\n- `src/unifyweaver/core/advanced/pattern_matchers.pl`",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      }
    ]
  }
}